A||||6||DR650SE||86 SE lost iol psi pulling g's?  Whats up with that?||||1||
Z||000000||DR650SE||11-05-2001||10:29 PM||||A few hours ago I was coming off a ramp that is fun to drive on.  The suggested speed limit was 25 so I was doing 50 because it is a round off ramp.  It's fun cuz I got huge sway bars and some nice shocks/struts and tires.  As I was almost through the ramp My car's oil light came on and the car died about 5 sec. later.  I wasn't able to get it started for about 15 min.  What happened?  Should I get the oil windage tray thingy from the fierostore to prevent this?  WHat should I do?  Thanks for the help.<BR>                                 DT<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
Z||000001||lowCG||11-05-2001||10:39 PM||||That oil pan baffle would help,welcome to the club!<BR>I've also heard of the Accusump accumulator used to help this also.||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||11-05-2001||10:57 PM||||There was a thread here not too long ago involving a Fiero that would show low oil press making sharp turns in a parking lot at even slow speeds. The puzzling part of your incident is why it died and wouldn't start right away. There is sme question whether the oil press switch will shut off the eng in the event of loss of oil press. I disconnected my oil press switch to see tonite, the eng kept running, oil light did come on.  (don't have a gauge) If your fuel pump relay is inoperative, the oil press switch will send a sig to run the fuel pump. If you lose oil press then, the eng will die from loss of fuel. With a bad FP relay, there is longer starting times, requiring oil press to build before the fuel pump will run. You might want to check the FP relay to see if it's working. Make sense? Anyway, sounds like the baffle will help, never had a problem myself of this kind.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DR650SE||11-05-2001||11:08 PM||||Thanks for the info.  Had I thought about it I would have realized that the oil pressure switch was wired to the FP Relay.  I have been meaning to change the fuel pump relay because It doesn't seem to work right.  It also makes it take a while to get started if the car hasn't run over night.  So I guess when it's cold out.  THanks for the info<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
Z||000004||maryjane||11-05-2001||11:32 PM||||DR650se, you have email at your address listed in your profile||||reg||1
Z||000005||grinthock||11-05-2001||11:50 PM||||I had that in my 85... OIL LEVEL LOW!!! Hard right hand turns will cause the oil to splash and if it's down 1 bottle, barly at the ADD mark that will happen....<P>that's my experience.||||reg||1
